  "id": "fourier-spectrum",
  "term": "Fourier spectrum",
  "definition": "In this context, the Fourier spectrum is the range of spatial frequency information that makes up an image. Researchers can filter an image to keep only a narrow band from this spectrum, such as low or high spatial frequencies, to study how different kinds of visual detail affect perception.",
